  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "Define \\(x \\otimes y = x^3 - y.\\) What is \\(h \\otimes (h \\otimes h)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-h\\)",
    "B": "\\(0\\)",
    "C": "\\(h\\)",
    "D": "\\(2h\\)",
    "E": "\\(h^3\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "First apply the rule to the operation inside the parentheses:\n\\[\nh\\otimes h=h^3-h.\n\\]\nFor the outer operation, the first input is \\(h\\) and the second input is the entire expression \\(h^3-h\\). Therefore\n\\[\nh\\otimes(h\\otimes h)\n=h^3-(h^3-h)\n=h^3-h^3+h=h.\n\\]\nThe result is \\(\\boxed{h}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
